# Scratch space for ci/report/publish-perf.py.  Nothing durable
# lives here: the record of the scheduled runs is kept at
# perf/history.jsonl on the gh-pages branch, and the badges the
# README links to are its siblings, perf/badge-*.json.
#
# What is committed on main is a placeholder -- an empty
# history.jsonl, so that a local or pull request docs build still
# renders a complete trend page, and a set of "no data" badges,
# which exist only so the unconditional copy-back in
# .github/actions/publish-perf has something to copy on the paths
# where publish-perf.py writes no badge at all.  Neither reaches
# the built site: the docs build publishes no static directory.
# The chart-*.html fragments are generated, and git-ignored.
#
# During a publishing run, and during the docs-deploy build, the
# real history is copied in here first and the tools work against
# it as if it had always been local.
#
# One workflow writes the record: system-tests.yml, whose three
# publishing lanes all go through .github/actions/publish-perf.
#   two-VM lane      perftest and iperf3   -> badge-rdma, badge-tcp
#   NVMe-oF lane     the fio sweep         -> badge-nvmeof
#   S3 lane          the GET size sweep    -> badge-s3
#
# Every record carries a "runner" field.  Numbers are only comparable
# within a class, so each class is charted and badged as its own
# series; the self-hosted records predate the move to hosted runners.
